OHOS: keep the scrolled application visible while a scrolling screenshot runs.
The compositor keeps this full-screen main window opaque, so the transparent
presentation that upstream uses for the scrolling hole cannot work and the
stitched frames only contained the frozen overlay. Hide the overlay for the
duration of the capture instead: the toolbar and the stitched-preview
thumbnail stay on screen, the pipeline sees the live window, and the wheel
reaches the application directly. The thumbnail becomes a parentless top-level
window on this platform so it survives the overlay hiding, and the first frame
is captured only after the window manager had a frame to remove the overlay.

